<?php

/**
 * @file
 * Install hooks for shh_facility_booking_cta.
 */

/**
 * Implements hook_install().
 *
 * Grants `create bee reservation` (bee's own permission, gating access to
 * `/node/{node}/add-reservation`) to the `authenticated` role.
 *
 * Found while implementing this task: no role on this site — not
 * `anonymous`, not `authenticated` — actually has this permission today.
 * Task 0012's (cart-hold concurrency prototype) own resolution notes
 * mention granting it *temporarily* to `anonymous` for a manual test and
 * explicitly reverting afterward, but nothing ever granted it permanently
 * to a real role. That means every previous "verified over real HTTP"
 * booking test in this project's history must have run as an admin/uid-1
 * session (which bypasses permission checks), not a realistic rider
 * account — a "Book now" link on the facility page would otherwise send
 * every real visitor straight to an Access Denied page, which would fail
 * this task's own "a rider can reach the booking form" acceptance
 * criterion.
 *
 * Granting to `authenticated` (not `anonymous`) matches decision 0017's
 * (anonymous-vs-authenticated booking access) exactly: authentication is
 * required before booking, anonymous browsing/availability viewing stays
 * open.
 */
function shh_facility_booking_cta_install() {
  user_role_grant_permissions('authenticated', ['create bee reservation']);
}
